      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T02:32:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is very Android specific, and makes this code hard to understand and reuse elsewere. Can we find a workflow that is more generic? I assume that 2 confirmations are required when the connection request is incoming from PTS-bot (and not outgoing), right?\n\nIf yes, can we hide this behavior in the `WaitConnection` method?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "badc860890bad10813d996c3c8c4c85f3f5b6dc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d4256a9_6fd182d1",
        "filename": "android/pandora/mmi2grpc/mmi2grpc/sm.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T08:04:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should put that in `WaitConnection`.\n\nI\u0027m not sure that this is very Android specific, but we shouldn\u0027t need to know the number of confirmations here.\n\nWhat we should do for me is just listen for pairing events in an async loop on the side and accept every numeric_comparaison PairingEvent.\n\nWe don\u0027t need to wait for the task to end as well.",
      "parentUuid": "97395fa1_9ffe7d6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "badc860890bad10813d996c3c8c4c85f3f5b6dc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "751e9b65_fa38dbc8",
        "filename": "android/pandora/mmi2grpc/mmi2grpc/sm.py",
